  "register": "notes",
  "source_dataset": "MIMIC_IV_NOTE",
  "text": "Allergies:\nAspirin / Penicillins / Codeine / Inderal / Isordil / Iodine; \nIodine Containing / Morphine / Celexa / Glucophage / \nAtorvastatin / Dilaudid / Vioxx / Levofloxacin / Hydralazine / \nOndansetron / Carbapenem / Lidocaine / Nortriptyline\n\nChief Complaint:\nabdominal pain\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\n___ MEDICINE ATTENDING ADMISSION NOTE \n \nDate: ___\nTime: 21:27\nPCP: ___: ___ \n\nThe patient is an ___ year old woman with a h/o coronary artery \ndisease, hypertension, type 2 diabetes, chronic renal \ninsufficiency, and a history of a cholecystectomy in ___, who \nhas had ongoing symptoms of right upper quadrant pain ever \nsince. \n\nShe was recently admitted (___) for abdominal \npain, which was evaluated by the GI consult service with MRCP \nfor possible chronic pancreatitis, which showed a normal bilary \nsystem in a post-cholecystectomy patient and a 1 cm dilated side \nbranch in the head of the pancreas which may represent a side \nbranch IPMN. She was started on a trial of ursodiol targeting \nthe possibility of lithogenic bile, continued on an aggressive \nbowel regimen and omeprazole for GERD. Also, her dicyclomine was \ndiscontinued at that time. \n\nShe now p/w with recurrent RUQ pain. She reports that she \ndiscontinued her ursodiol due to increased abdominal pain, which \nshe attributed to the medication, but is not sure. She also \nendorses vertigo for the past 2 weeks, which improves with \nmeclizine, but she had to discontinue because it upset her \nstomach. She is followed by GI as an outpatient. She also \nendorses diarrhea, nausea, a decreased PO intake, urinary \nfrequency and dysurea for the past several days. She denies cp \nand sob.\n \n\nIn ER: \nVS: 98 80 117/61 16 97%RA\nStudies: labs reveal ARF \nFluids given: 500 cc NS\nMeds given: tylenol ___ mg po x 1\nConsults called: GI (fellow Dr. ___ recommended admit \npatient for inpatient MRA/MRI)\n\nShe also reported urethral pain from the catheterization in the \nED, which has now subsided.\n \nReview of Systems:  \n(+) Per HPI  \n(-) Denies fever, chills, night sweats, recent weight loss or \ngain. Denies visual changes, headache, sinus tenderness, \nrhinorrhea, congestion or sore throat. Denies chest pain or \ntightness, palpitations, orthopnea, dyspnea on exertion. Denies \ncough, shortness of breath, wheezes or pleuritic pain. Denies \nnausea, vomiting, diarrhea, constipation, BRBPR, melena, or \nabdominal pain. No dysuria, urinary frequency. Denies \narthralgias or myalgias. Denies rashes. No numbness/tingling or \nmuscle weakness in extremities. No feelings of depression or \nanxiety. All other review of systems negative.\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\n___ h/o CAD, HTN, DM, asymptomatic bradycardia, with a recent \nadmission from ___ for RUQ abdominal pain, who now p/w \nrecurrent epigastric pain.\n\nAbdominal pain, recurrent: Unknown etiology of abdominal pain. \nThe patient has undergone a very extensive workup.  Her pain may \nbe phantom gall bladder pain given her history of pain beginning \nafter cholecystectomy.  GI was consulted and outpatient MRE and \nMRA that had been ordered were performed inpatient which \nrevealed a duodenal diverticula but no other pathology.  Her \npain improved somewhat with tylenol.  Gastroenterology will \nfollow up on the abdominal pain syndrome and MRI findings as an \noutpatient - appointments have been arranged. \n\nACUTE ON CHRONIC RENAL FAILURE: improved with rehydration.\n\nURINARY TRACTION INFECTION: Proteus UTI resistent to bactirm and \ncipro.  She has allergies to cephalosporins and penicillins, so \nthe only option was to treat with tobramycin, which was used for \nthis infection.  Her urinary tract infection improved.  She was \ngiven 1 L IVF daily while getting tobramycin to reduce risk of \nrenal failure or ototoxicity.  Her creatinine remained stable \nthroughout the hospitalization. \n\nCAD/HTN/DM: Stable. continued home ticlopidine 250 mg 1 po BID, \nsimvastatin 40 mg 1 po daily, enalapril maleate 5 mg 1 po daily, \nglargine insulin 15 U QHS and SSI.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nPrimary Diagnosis: \nAcute on Chronic abdominal pain\nUrinary tract infection",
